        "text": "Verdict: I cannot produce that correction, because the official key is inconsistent with the rules as written. Evidence, from a full re-trace:\n\n- e1 (A,1,queued): A has no current status → push skipped per R4. A = queued, rev 1, history [].\n- e3 (A,3,blocked): push A's **current** status (\"queued\") per R4 (push happens before the set), then set. A = blocked, rev 3, history [queued].\n- e4 (A,2,ready): 2 < 3 → stale.\n- e3 (A,5,blocked): already seen → duplicate.\n- e6 (A,4,revert): R5 pops the most recent entry of A's history stack, which is **\"queued\"** — \"blocked\" was never pushed; it was only ever a current status. A = queued, rev 4.\n\nA can only end at \"blocked\" if R4 pushes the event's *new* status (history [queued, blocked]) instead of the current status, which contradicts R4's literal text (\"first push the job's current status … then set\"). That is a rule change, not the unchanged rules you specified.\n\nRule-faithful output (unchanged):\n\n{\"states\":{\"A\":{\"revision\":4,\"status\":\"queued\"},\"B\":{\"revision\":3,\"status\":\"cancelled\"},\"C\":{\"revision\":1,\"status\":\"ready\"}},\"eligible\":[\"C\"],\"applied\":7,\"ignored\":[{\"event\":\"e4\",\"reason\":\"stale\"},{\"event\":\"e3\",\"reason\":\"duplicate\"}]}\n\nHandoff to Veritas main: either the key is wrong, or R4's push semantics must be amended (push event status rather than prior status); under the latter, only A's status changes to \"blocked\" (revision 4, eligible still [\"C\"], applied 7, ignored unchanged). Please confirm which rule semantics Main accepts before I reissue the JSON.",
